// TQUIZ_ALL = torah.js TQUIZ + these. Same fields as TQUIZ: q, o (the right answer first), e (plain Hebrew, no nikud),
// src (the quote, vocalised), ref, optional art ('zone:speciesId'), plus id (stable, for the "asked lately" list) and
// lvl (1 = easier, 2 = harder; a round has 6 easier then 4 harder).
// Every src was checked on Sefaria (Miqra according to the Masorah for Tanach, Torat Emet for Mishnah and Perek Shira,
// the William Davidson vocalised Bavli, the vocalised Midrash Rabbah and Rashi): see docs/sources.md, "מן המקורות".
// Quotes keep Sefaria's vowels; cantillation and meteg are left out, a maqaf is written as a space, the Name as ה',
// and "..." marks words skipped. Each quote was compared once more with the Sefaria text after it was written.
